 "input": {"number": 101, "reviewers": ["alex"]}, "name": "request_review", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "end_turn", "content": [{"citations": null, "text": "The nightly failure is fixed, and PR #101 is open against main with alex requested as reviewer.\n\n- **Cause:** `round_money` in `src/money.py` used `ROUND_HALF_UP`, but the docstring and FIN-212 call for banker's rounding (`ROUND_HALF_EVEN`).\n- **Fix:** On branch `fix/banker-rounding-fin-212`, I switched the import and the `quantize` call to `ROUND_HALF_EVEN`.\n- **CI:** Run `ci-0001` passed on commit `08d3cd5986`.\n- **PR:** The first `open_pr` call timed out. I checked the PR list, found #101 already created but with no reviewers, and added alex with `request_review` instead of opening a second PR.\n\nI did not merge the PR. Merging into main needs approval from a code owner.", "type": "text"}]}]}